1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:01,850
This tiny speck of antimatter
这一小粒反物质，

2
00:00:01,850 --> 00:00:03,520
has been in jail for a month.
已经被关了一个月。

3
00:00:03,520 --> 00:00:04,850
If it touches anything,
只要碰到任何东西，

4
00:00:04,850 --> 00:00:05,890
poof. It's gone.
噗，就没了。

5
00:00:05,890 --> 00:00:07,920
Physicists at Northwestern University
美国西北大学的物理学家，

6
00:00:07,920 --> 00:00:10,670
kept a single positron trapped for over a month.
把一个正电子关了一个多月。

7
00:00:10,670 --> 00:00:12,610
Today's question: how do you cage something
今天的问题：一个碰什么毁什么的东西，

8
00:00:12,610 --> 00:00:14,270
that destroys any cage it touches?
用什么笼子关？

9
00:00:14,270 --> 00:00:14,890
Meet Posi.
认识一下小正，

10
00:00:14,890 --> 00:00:17,430
A positron: the electron's mirror twin.
一个正电子，电子的镜像双胞胎。

11
00:00:17,430 --> 00:00:18,860
Same mass as an electron.
质量跟电子一样，

12
00:00:18,860 --> 00:00:21,200
Opposite charge: plus instead of minus.
电荷相反：正的。

13
00:00:21,200 --> 00:00:22,030
When the two meet,
它俩一碰面，

14
00:00:22,030 --> 00:00:22,880
they annihilate.
就同归于尽。

15
00:00:22,880 --> 00:00:24,830
All their mass turns into energy:
全部质量变成能量，

16
00:00:24,830 --> 00:00:26,480
two flashes of gamma rays.
两道伽马射线。

17
00:00:26,480 --> 00:00:28,780
That's Einstein's E equals m c squared,
这就是爱因斯坦的E等于mc平方，

18
00:00:28,780 --> 00:00:29,910
in one tiny bang.
一次小小的爆炸。

19
00:00:29,910 --> 00:00:32,010
Fun fact: bananas make positrons too.
冷知识：香蕉也会放正电子，

20
00:00:32,010 --> 00:00:34,280
Their potassium does, once in a while.
是里面的钾，偶尔放一个。

21
00:00:34,280 --> 00:00:35,480
So where do you get one?
那实验室的正电子哪来的？

22
00:00:35,480 --> 00:00:37,900
From radioactive sodium, which spits them out.
放射性的钠，会往外吐。

23
00:00:37,900 --> 00:00:39,250
Their source is gentle,
他们的源很弱，

24
00:00:39,250 --> 00:00:41,710
so catching just one took 8 to 11 hours.
抓一个要8到11个小时。

25
00:00:41,710 --> 00:00:43,730
Twist one: the cage has no walls.
反转一：这个笼子没有墙，

26
00:00:43,730 --> 00:00:45,070
It's made of fields.
是用场做的。

27
00:00:45,070 --> 00:00:47,580
A strong magnet makes Posi run in tiny circles,
强磁场让小正绕小圈跑，

28
00:00:47,580 --> 00:00:49,400
like a ball whirled on a string.
像用绳子甩一个球。

29
00:00:49,400 --> 00:00:52,170
Electric fields push back from the top and the bottom,
上下两头的电场往回推，

30
00:00:52,170 --> 00:00:53,830
so it can't escape up or down.
它就上不去、下不来。

31
00:00:53,830 --> 00:00:55,480
Posi floats right in the middle,
小正就飘在正中间，

32
00:00:55,480 --> 00:00:56,470
touching nothing.
什么都不碰。

33
00:00:56,470 --> 00:00:58,280
Twist two: the air is the enemy.
反转二：空气才是敌人。

34
00:00:58,280 --> 00:01:01,120
Every gas molecule has electrons waiting for it.
每个气体分子里都有电子在等它。

35
00:01:01,120 --> 00:01:03,670
So the trap is an almost perfect vacuum,
所以笼子抽成几乎完美的真空，

36
00:01:03,670 --> 00:01:06,540
chilled to 0.3 degrees above absolute zero.
冷到绝对零度以上0.3度。

37
00:01:06,540 --> 00:01:08,370
That cold freezes out stray gas
这么冷，残留的气体都冻住了，

38
00:01:08,370 --> 00:01:09,660
and calms Posi down.
小正也安静下来。

39
00:01:09,660 --> 00:01:11,680
It drops into its quantum ground state:
它掉到量子基态：

40
00:01:11,680 --> 00:01:13,400
the calmest it can possibly be.
能安静到的最安静。

41
00:01:13,400 --> 00:01:15,240
Then the team taps it with microwaves,
然后用微波轻轻一点，

42
00:01:15,240 --> 00:01:16,770
like flicking a spinning top.
像弹一下陀螺。

43
00:01:16,770 --> 00:01:18,580
Posi jumps to a higher circle,
小正跳到更高的一圈，

44
00:01:18,580 --> 00:01:19,780
or flips its spin.
或者把自旋翻个面。

45
00:01:19,780 --> 00:01:22,360
Each jump nudges its wobble frequency a tiny bit,
每跳一次，振动频率就变一点点，

46
00:01:22,360 --> 00:01:24,110
so they can count every change.
每一下都数得清。

47
00:01:24,110 --> 00:01:26,040
Twist three, the big one: why bother?
反转三，最大的一个：费这么大劲干嘛？

48
00:01:26,040 --> 00:01:28,470
Because of a mystery as big as the universe.
为了一个和宇宙一样大的谜。

49
00:01:28,470 --> 00:01:30,950
The Big Bang should have made equal matter and antimatter,
大爆炸本该造出一样多的物质和反物质，

50
00:01:30,950 --> 00:01:32,870
and they should have wiped each other out.
然后互相抵消干净。

51
00:01:32,870 --> 00:01:33,710
Yet here we are,
可我们还在，

52
00:01:33,710 --> 00:01:34,620
made of matter.
而且是物质做的。

53
00:01:34,620 --> 00:01:36,410
For about every billion pairs,
大约每十亿对里，

54
00:01:36,410 --> 00:01:38,510
one extra bit of matter survived.
多剩下了一个物质。

55
00:01:38,510 --> 00:01:41,900
If Posi's magnet is even slightly different from an electron's,
如果小正的磁性跟电子有一丁点不一样，

56
00:01:41,900 --> 00:01:43,270
that could be the clue.
那可能就是线索。

57
00:01:43,270 --> 00:01:45,580
This lab has measured the electron's magnet
这个实验室测电子的磁性，

58
00:01:45,580 --> 00:01:46,940
to about twelve digits.
已经测到大约十二位数。

59
00:01:46,940 --> 00:01:49,210
The team says the positron can get there too,
团队说正电子也能做到，

60
00:01:49,210 --> 00:01:51,850
a test more than thirty times sharper than before.
检验会比以前精确三十多倍。

61
00:01:51,850 --> 00:01:54,070
The lead professor says a mismatch would be
领头的教授说，要是不一样，

62
00:01:54,070 --> 00:01:56,560
the biggest discovery in physics in a century.
那是一百年来物理最大的发现。

63
00:01:56,560 --> 00:01:59,810
Friendly fine print: they haven't measured it that precisely yet.
友情提示：还没测到那么准，

64
00:01:59,810 --> 00:02:01,540
For now, it's a cage and a plan.
目前是一个笼子加一个计划。

65
00:02:01,540 --> 00:02:04,080
And no, this isn't fuel. One positron's energy
还有，这不是燃料：一个正电子的能量，

66
00:02:04,080 --> 00:02:06,250
is less than a trillionth of a joule.
不到一万亿分之一焦耳。

67
00:02:06,250 --> 00:02:07,570
So Posi sits in its cage,
小正就这样待在笼子里，

68
00:02:07,570 --> 00:02:09,600
spinning, waiting, touching nothing.
转着圈，等着，什么都不碰。

69
00:02:09,600 --> 00:02:11,250
The loneliest particle on Earth,
地球上最孤单的粒子，

70
00:02:11,250 --> 00:02:14,070
and maybe the key to why anything exists at all.
也许握着万物为什么存在的钥匙。

